Mauga...

Thanks for the reply.  The percentages range from .01 to .30.  They represent a selection of the bottom range of wider distribution.  They could be considered as a truncated normal, I suppose.  In setting up the equations for the intercept and slope for the gcm, the measurement equations would be

int =~ 1*y1 + 1*y2 + 1*y3...
slp =~ 0*y1 + 1*y2 + 2*y3 ...

How would I set the string priors to specify the distribution of the y's?

Thanks

David

